OpenVmfs is an independent implementation. It contains no source code from other VMFS or VMDK implementations.
It was written by people who had read those implementations, not in a clean room; an audit of the code against
them (2026-11) found no copied or translated code and led to the removal of identifier names that had been taken
over from dissect.vmfs.

VMware publishes no specification of VMFS. What is known about the format comes from the people who studied it
before us, and we read their work to learn it. We thank the authors of:

  - dissect.vmfs and dissect.hypervisor (Fox-IT / NCC Group, AGPL-3.0-or-later)
  - vmfs-tools (Christophe Fillot, Mike Hommey, GPL-2.0-or-later)
  - vmfs6-tools and vmfs6-tool (Weafon Tsao, Thomas Ward, Philipp Herkert and others, GPL-2.0-or-later)
  - fvmfs, the Open Source VMFS Driver (fluid Operations, GPL-3.0)
  - QEMU's VMDK block driver (block/vmdk.c, MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2004 Fabrice Bellard, Copyright (c) 2005
    Filip Navara), including its description of the SESparse format. The checks OpenVmfs makes on a SESparse
    header are the ones that driver makes.
  - libvmdk's format documentation (Joachim Metz, GFDL-1.3-or-later)

docs/format/sources.md lists what was learned from each of them. The format description in docs/format is written
in our own words and checked against volumes written by ESXi.

